  "description": "Decision 266's kernel-code probe (phase1.25_pilot-wand item 2.7: the infinite ring tap by tap), exploratory: the P-tie mesh of export-padding-tie-512; document resolution 512. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
